From 94f06bf94693f1b9fdc3a78c182474b6d2124670 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gili Tzabari <cowwoc2020@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 13:55:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(ci): bound macOS daemon fixture disk usage

Run macOS CLI integration tests one at a time so packaged daemon fixtures
do not materialize independent full CLI copies concurrently. Keep the
existing test payloads, assertions and timeouts, and retain normal test
concurrency on other platforms.

Base: rust-v0.163.0 (83086188ae0614bd882818ff1aa23f3194962012) with queue through 0067.
Red: full Bazel run 39022737141, ARM job 117367848543, two packaged daemon
tests fail with No space left on device (os error 28).
Green: native run 39036837568 executes 14 packaged/lifecycle tests and 12
daemon startup tests on each macOS architecture, all passing. Generated
target query confirms both CLI labels receive --test-threads=1.
Maintained just fmt-check passes. Fresh emitted and full CI gates remain pending.
---
 codex-rs/cli/BUILD.bazel | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/codex-rs/cli/BUILD.bazel b/codex-rs/cli/BUILD.bazel
index 8d57048a5..f89edd3a6 100644
--- a/codex-rs/cli/BUILD.bazel
+++ b/codex-rs/cli/BUILD.bazel
@@ -11,6 +11,11 @@ codex_rust_crate(
     extra_binaries = [
         "//codex-rs/bwrap:bwrap",
     ],
+    # Packaged daemon fixtures each materialize independent copies of the CLI.
+    integration_test_args = select({
+        "@platforms//os:macos": ["--test-threads=1"],
+        "//conditions:default": [],
+    }),
     integration_test_timeouts = {
         "cli-app_server_daemon-test": "moderate",
     },
-- 
2.43.0

